\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Two generator choices at the zero label}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{At momentum zero on a grid with two equal-period directions
#{a,b}, their quarter-turn fixes the label. For a graded spin
carrier as in \ref{fdip-016X}, take the cyclic subgroup
generated by #{u_{ab}} and the root
#{\zeta=(1+\ui)/\sqrt{2}}. A vector on which #{u_{ab}} has
multiplier #{\zeta} has degree #{1} for this generator. Such vectors occur
because #{\varepsilon_a}
exchanges the two eigenspaces of #{\varepsilon_a\varepsilon_b}
at #{\pm\ui}, as in the calculation of \ref{fdip-016Y}.
Choosing #{u_{ab}^{-1}} for the same subgroup gives that vector
degree #{-1}. Both [generator choices](fdip-0173) refer to the
same zero block. Its equality with the opposite block fixes
neither choice.}
